this week the senate is expected to  confirm the first black woman to serve  on the supreme court the judiciary  committee meets this morning for a vote  to send judge katanji brown jackson's  nomination to the senate floor now if  she is confirmed it's likely to be with  almost no republican support nicole  killian is covering brown's confirmation  process nicole good morning to you so  what do we expect this morning's vote  how do we expect it to go  well gale judge katanji brown jackson  appears to have enough support to get  confirmed to the supreme court by the  senate by the end of this week but her  first hurdle will be getting out of the  senate judiciary committee which is  expected to vote today on party lines  some republicans on the panel who tried  to press the judge during her  confirmation hearings have already said  they'll oppose her citing her judicial  philosophy and some of her sentencing  decisions if the committee splits in a  tie democrats can still advance her  nomination and are planning a floor vote  later this week jackson is expected to  have the backing of democrats and at  least one republican maine senator susan  collins which would allow her to be  confirmed with at least some bipartisan  support a senior white house adviser  tells me that they still believe there  are some undecided gop lawmakers out  there that they hope to get which is why  judge jackson will be back on the hill  this week meeting with more senators  ahead of the final vote nate  we shall see nicole thank you
 

